etym.Dean:
{{dercat|en|la-med|gkm}}
The surname or given name is of multiple origins, depending on context:

* As an English surname, from {{der|en|enm|dene|t=valley}}.
* Also as an English surname, from the noun {{m|en|dean}}. Cognate to {{m|en|Deacon}}.
* Also as an English surname, from the personal name {{m|en|Deyne}}, a rhyming form of {{m|en|Reynald}} (see {{m|en|Reginald}}).
* As an {{der|en|ga|-}} surname, variant of {{m|en|Deane}}.
* As a Scottish surname, from {{w|Dean Castle}} in [[Kilmarnock]], itself from the noun meaning valley.
* {{inh|en|ang|Dene||Dane, Norseman}}
* {{der|en|he|דין||law, judgment}} and {{der|en|ar|دين||way of life, creed}}

