etym.Gordon:
The main etymology, associated with {{der|en|cel|-}} names, is from the {{bor|en|sco|-}} surname {{m|sco|Gordon}}, from a place name, but the origin is {{unc|en|debated}}:
* If the English or Scots name is from a {{der|en|cel-bry|-}} language (such as {{der|en|owl|-}} or {{der|en|obt|-}}), then possibly from a {{der|en|cel-bry-pro|-}} compound such as {{com|cel-bry-pro|*gor|*din|t1=spacious|t2=fort|nocat=1}};
* If the Scots name is itself from English, then possibly from {{der|en|fr|Gourdon}}, derived from Gallo-Roman {{der|en|la|Gordus}}, from {{der|en|cel-gau||*Gordos}};
* Otherwise, possibly ultimately from {{uder|en|ang|*gordūn|*gor-dūn|mud hill}}{{attn|ang|attested??}} whence a habitati

