etym.Trent:
{{swp|River +}}
{{inh+|en|enm|Trent}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Trēonte}}; Koch (2006) derives the river name from {{der|en|cel-pro|*tri-sent(o)-on-ā-}}, from the elements {{m|cel-pro|*trei||through}} + {{m|cel-pro|*sentus||path}}. Traditionally said to be from {{der|en|cel-bry-pro|-}} elements equivalent to {{m|cy|tros||over}} + {{m|cy|hynt||way}}, often taken to mean "the {{l|en|trespasser}}"

The surname in some cases is a shortening of "{{m|en|Tranent}}", or "{{m|en|Tranant}}" in {{der|en|gd|-}}, a geographical location in {{l|en|East Lothian}}. "Tranant" itself is possibly of {{m|en|Brythonic}} {{gloss|{{der|en|cel|-}}}} origin.

